     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hello Filipe,<div><br></div><div>Actually I want to count &quot;plot-wise green pixel&quot; from the orthomosaic for plant vigor estimation.</div><div>I have tried different code for this purpose but wasn&#39;t effective in the sense had much problem in ortho format conversion and all. So I would like to modify the FIELDimageR code, </div><div>Which has mentioned below:</div><div><br></div><div><div><br></div><div><div>EX1&lt;-stack(&quot;EX1_RGB.tif&quot;)</div><div>plotRGB(EX1, r = 1, g = 2, b = 3)</div><div><br></div><div>EX1.RemSoil&lt;- fieldMask(mosaic = EX1, Red = 1, Green = 2, Blue = 3, index = &quot;SCI&quot;)</div><div><br></div><div>EX1.Shape&lt;-fieldShape(mosaic = EX1.RemSoil,ncols = 1, nrows = 6)</div><div><br></div><div>### Field map identification (name for each Plot). &#39;fieldPlot&#39; argument can be a number or name.</div><div><br></div><div>DataTable&lt;-read.csv(&quot;DataTable.csv&quot;,header = T)  </div><div>fieldMap&lt;-fieldMap(fieldPlot=DataTable$Plot, fieldRange=DataTable$Range, fieldRow=DataTable$Row, decreasing=T)</div><div>fieldMap</div><div><br></div><div># The new column PlotName is identifying the plots:</div><div>EX1.Shape&lt;-fieldShape(mosaic = EX1.RemSoil, ncols = 1, nrows = 6, fieldMap = fieldMap)</div><div><br></div><div>### Joing all information in one &quot;fieldShape&quot; file:</div><div><br></div><div>EX1.Shape&lt;-fieldShape(mosaic = EX1.RemSoil, ncols = 1, nrows = 6, fieldMap = fieldMap, </div><div>                      fieldData = DataTable, ID = &quot;Plot&quot;)</div><div><br></div><div># The new column PlotName is identifying the plots:                      </div><div>EX1.Shape$fieldShape@data </div></div><div><br></div></div><div>How can I modify the above code, so I&#39;ll get &quot;:green pixel count&quot; after soil removal from ortho??</div><div>objective is that to differentiate plot on early plant vigor. for that I have two different plot ortho&#39;s which has much difference in NDVI values likewise plot1 =0.76 &amp; plot2= 0.85</div><div><br></div><div>KIndly suggest me,</div><div><br></div><div>I&#39;ve attached both plot for you reference</div><div><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/10c1sgN_LBj2bYiWRm40K-RAWmTLD6SlF\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/10c1sgN_LBj2bYiWRm40K-RAWmTLD6SlF&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242205669000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3QUp4LI4jeOOZzF9DQhE0L\">https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/10c1sgN_LBj2bYiWRm40K-RAWmTLD6SlF</a><br></div><div><br></div><div>Thank you,</div><div>Sudhir.</div><div><br></div><div> </div></div>"
